  "source_code": "# cook your dish here\r\nT = int(input())\r\n\r\nfor _ in range(T):\r\n    n = int(input())\r\n    a = list(map(int, input().split()))\r\n    \r\n    a.sort(reverse=True)\r\n    pref = [0] * (3 * n + 1)\r\n    \r\n    for i in range(3 * n):\r\n        pref[i+1] = pref[i] + a[i]\r\n        \r\n    answer = 0\r\n    \r\n    for i in range(n + 1):\r\n        low =0\r\n        high = n - i\r\n        \r\n        while low < high:\r\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\r\n            q = i + 2 * mid\r\n            r = 3 * n - 2 * i - mid\r\n            \r\n            change = a[q] + a[q + 1] - 3 * a[r - 1]\r\n            \r\n            if change > 0:\r\n                low = mid +1\r\n            else:\r\n                high = mid\r\n        \r\n        for j in (low, max(0, low - 1)):\r\n            \r\n            if j > n - i:\r\n                continue\r\n            \r\n            q = i + 2 * j\r\n            r = 3 * n - 2 * i - j\r\n            \r\n            current = (6 * pref[i] + 4 * (pref[q] - pref[i]) + 3 * (pref[r] - pref[q]))\r\n            \r\n            answer = max(answer, current)\r\n    print(answer)",
